        consequence: 'Frozen-fry brands vary in parboil depth, starch content, and thickness. McCain steak-cut fries need a different time than Ore-Ida shoestring fries, and store-brand fries might be par-fried differently. Starting with your usual 14–16 minutes can result in burnt edges and soft centers, or vice versa.',
        prevention: 'Start a new brand at 12 minutes, shake at 5 and 10, check for doneness (break one open and check the interior), then note the actual finish time for future batches.',
