      'Oil spray both sides with a light hand, applied immediately before cooking. Even though the sticks are pre-breaded from manufacturing, a thin layer of oil helps the Maillard reaction and prevents breading from drying into a chalky, crumbly texture instead of remaining crispy and cohesive. The oil should appear as a light sheen, not dripping.',
