      'Perforated or mesh baskets are essential, not optional. Dumplings are small and compact; a solid basket or flat tray can develop low points where dumplings sag and trap moisture underneath. A perforated basket allows steam to escape from beneath, keeping the entire bottom surface exposed to circulating air instead of resting on a moisture-trapping surface.',
      'Spacing logic differs from larger foods. Frozen dumplings can be placed closer together than mozzarella sticks because their filling is fully sealed inside (no rupture risk from radiant heat) and they don\'t expand during cooking. You can densely fill the basket with minimal spacing, but avoid overlapping—contact points will steam and remain pale instead of crisping.',
      'Probe placement for internal temperature is tricky with dumplings because of their size. Rather than inserting a probe into a whole dumpling, break open the largest or most central one and check the internal flesh of the filling visually or by placing an instant-read thermometer in the opening. The wrapper and filling heat at different rates, so probing through the wrapper may give a surface reading rather than the filling\'s true center temperature.',
