      'Skip the extra oil mist unless you specifically want more color — commercial tots are already pre-fried and carry a manufactured fat coating in the shell, so added oil mostly pools in the grooves between shredded potato strands rather than improving crispness, and can tip into greasiness.',
      'If your unit leans more radiant-heating (like a toaster-oven-style air fryer) than fan-forced, expect the top-facing side of each tot to color faster than the bottom regardless of basket position, so plan on redistributing the pile rather than assuming one shake evens out both heating styles equally.',
      'When tots are stacked two layers deep, toss and fully redistribute the pile rather than just jostling the basket — a light jostle resettles tots back into roughly the same stack, leaving the same tots buried against their neighbors for the whole cook.',
