      'Look at the ridged edges where shredded potato strands poke out from the rounder body — those edges brown and darken noticeably faster than the smoother curved sides, so a properly done batch shows darker freckled ridges against a lighter gold body rather than uniform color everywhere.',
      'Press one gently with tongs — a done tot resists with a light crackling give and holds its shape, while one that dents inward like a soft dumpling still has a cold or mushy center underneath the shell.',
      'Break one open and check the interior — it should be opaque, fluffy, and steaming hot all the way through; a grayish, translucent, or still-cool center means that tot didn\'t get enough exposure.',
