    technicalDeepDive: 'Commercial tater tots arrive pre-fried and frozen, so the shredded potato starch inside is already gelatinized and coated in a thin fat layer from manufacturing — the air fryer\'s job is to re-crisp that shell, not cook the interior from raw. A chunk of the early minutes at 400°F goes into converting surface ice back to liquid and driving it off as vapor, since that phase change must finish before the exterior can climb into Maillard territory. Packing tots in a single or double layer matters because each puff blocks hot air from its neighbors, so spacing them lets the fan strip the humid boundary layer fast enough for the crust to turn brittle instead of staying soft and steamed.',

