      'Crust firmness under pressure: At the target pull temperature of 130°F, press your fingertip against the crust edge. It should feel like a taut muscle - firm but not hard, with a slight give. Soft or squishy signals undercooking; rock-hard signals the steak is at or past medium and will taste dry after resting.',
      'Flesh translucency at the edge: Look at the cooked-side edge of the steak during the flips - the flesh should gradually shift from red to pink to opaque as the minutes pass. At pull time, the outer quarter of the cross-section should be opaque; if it is still very pink throughout, the center is underdone and needs more time.',
      'Juice accumulation and clarity: As you baste in the final minutes, clear amber liquid should gradually pool in the pan\'s low spots. If juices never accumulate or appear cloudy-gray, the steak is not cooking evenly through its thickness and the center temperature is climbing unevenly.',
