    technicalDeepDive: 'This stage is really about the physics of shredded cheese, since the beef and beans underneath already crossed their safety thresholds on the stovetop. Cheese is an emulsion of fat and casein protein suspended in water; as it heats, the casein network loosens and the whole structure flows, which reads as melting, but push it too far and the proteins tighten back up while the fat separates out into a greasy layer. A cheese blend hedges against that, since different cheeses reach flow and breakdown at different points. The chips underneath crisp mainly by losing surface moisture to the dry oven air faster than the cheese blanket above them can trap it in.',
