      'The tortilla surface will lose its white frost (frozen surface) very quickly (within 1 minute) and then transition from pale to cream-colored to light gold; once the tips of the taquito turn light amber, the filling is typically approaching 165°F inside. The timing from pale to amber is usually 5–6 minutes.',
      'Audible crunch appears when you move the taquito with tongs around the 6-minute mark; the earlier silence of a thawing tortilla suddenly becomes a crunching sound as the tortilla structure dries and the starches set. This sound is a more reliable signal than color, since lighting varies.',
      'Steam will rise from the basket fairly steadily through the first 5–6 minutes (from the filling thawing and the internal meat cooking), then taper; once steam drops noticeably around minute 7, the internal temperature is likely approaching 165°F and the tortilla is nearly fully crisped. Heavy steam at minute 8 signals that the filling is still frozen or the tortilla is not drying fast enough.',
