        prevention: 'Homemade or artisanal tortillas can take 10–12 minutes at 380°F due to higher thickness and water content; pre-test one taquito and assess crisping time before cooking a full batch. If time exceeds 12 minutes, lower temperature to 360°F and extend time by 2–3 minutes to allow the thicker tortilla to brown without the filling overheating.',
