      'The 270°F temperature is low enough that eggs rest directly on the basket floor without any protective insert; no parchment is needed and would actually impede the air circulation that keeps the heating gentle and even.',
      'Fork pricks should be 6-8 tiny punctures distributed around the circumference of the shell, not one deep stab. Shallow pricks vent steam as it forms, preventing uneven pressure buildup that can split the shell in places where the puncture did not reach.',
      'A silicone mat or foil sheet under the eggs prevents stray shell fragments from falling through the basket and burning on the heating element, which matters only if a crack occurs during cooking—not preventative, but protective if needed.',
      'Air fryer temperature must be fully stabilized before eggs enter; inserting eggs into a chamber that is still ramping up to 270°F reintroduces the sudden heat stress the low-temperature method is designed to avoid.',
      'Eggs should lie flat or nestle naturally in the basket; stacking or crowding creates uneven heat exposure and means pressure from one egg bears against another, forcing the shell to yield where it is thinnest rather than where you pocked it.',
