    uniqueSensoryCues: [
      'A properly finished cannellini bean should mash easily against the side of the pot under light spoon pressure but still hold its shape sitting in the bowl. Beans that dissolve into the broth entirely on their own, with no pressure needed, have gone past tender into overcooked.',
      'The chili\'s body should visibly thicken and pick up a slightly glossy sheen on the surface as bean starch releases into the broth, rather than staying thin with beans floating loose in watery liquid.',
      'Ground turkey should stay visible as small, distinct crumbles suspended through the chili rather than dissolving into an indistinct mass blended with the beans. If the meat has bound together into a paste, it was likely browned into overly fine crumbles or stirred too aggressively.',
      'Late in the cook, the steam rising off the pot should carry a rounder, blended cumin-and-chile aroma rather than a raw, dusty spice smell, which signals the seasoning hasn\'t fully opened up into the broth yet.',
    ],
