    technicalDeepDive: 'Dropping frozen pierogi into gently boiling water means the first energy reaching the dough goes into melting the ice locked inside the potato-cheese filling before the interior temperature can climb at all, which is why the exterior can look nearly finished well before the center is actually hot. A gentle boil rather than a hard one matters because the raw seam is still soft and only partially set at this stage, and turbulent water finds any weak point in the crimp before the surface starch has fully gelatinized into a sealed skin. Once that skin sets and steam builds enough to overcome the dumpling\'s density, it rises and stays at the surface.',
    keywords: ['how long to boil pierogies', 'frozen pierogies cook time', 'boiling frozen pierogies', 'mrs ts pierogies cooking time', 'perogies boil time'],
