      'Choose a heavy-bottomed saucepan rather than a thin one. With only 3 cups of liquid for 1 cup of lentils, the liquid layer at the pot\'s bottom gets shallow well before the lentils are done, and a thin pot develops a hot spot right there that scorches the bottom layer before the rest of the batch finishes.',
      'Expect a thin gray foam on the surface during the first few minutes of the boil — this is surface starch and material shed from the seed coats. Skim it off if you plan to keep the cooking liquid for a soup base; otherwise it\'s harmless and simmers back in on its own.',
