      'Position a meat thermometer probe in the absolute center of the thickest part of the roast, not in a pocket of fat or near the edge. The thermometer should be inserted horizontally through the side of the roast if possible, avoiding bone and aiming for pure muscle. This placement means the probe reads the slowest-cooking part of the roast, giving you the most reliable doneness signal.',
