      'Watch the color boundary where the meat meets the exposed cross-section of bone. As heat penetrates, a visible gradient will form with grey-cooked meat expanding inward and pink-raw meat shrinking. When the pink zone is gone and the entire cross-section is uniformly grey, the marrow is nearly liquid.',
      'The braising liquid should take on a glossy, slightly silky sheen by 90 minutes into the braise. This sheen comes from emulsified rendered fat and collagen gelatin rising off the bones. If the liquid remains thin and watery at that point, either the pot is leaking steam or the heat is too low and the meat is merely stewing rather than braising.',
      'The marrow\'s color shift is the most reliable doneness signal. It starts dark red from blood and hemoglobin, then gradually turns light grey-brown as the inside heats. When a small spoon meets almost no resistance and the marrow looks uniformly grey throughout, it is fully liquid and ready to pull from the bone at the table.',
