        q: 'Can I use oil instead of butter?',
        a: 'Oil works but lacks flavor and its higher smoke point means you might creep over 300°F without noticing. Butter browns around 350°F, which serves as a natural alarm if the pan gets too hot. Oil is forgiving on heat but gives you no visual warning.',
