        q: 'What is the real difference between blackened and charred?',
        a: 'Charred means burnt, unintentional, and tastes acrid. Blackened means the spice coating has undergone controlled thermal decomposition at high heat, creating edible char with specific flavor compounds from paprika and other spices. If it tastes burnt or acrid, the heat was too high or the cook time too long. Blackened should taste intense, smoky, and intentional.',
