    technicalDeepDive: 'Shallow frying transfers heat by conduction through oil, which has far greater heat capacity and more even contact with the cutlet\'s surface than a dry pan does, so the submerged face heats faster and more uniformly than pan-searing alone allows. The breading acts as a buffer: the egg and crumb layer dehydrates and browns through the Maillard reaction while partly insulating the meat underneath, moderating how fast moisture escapes the cutlet even as the crust colors. Because the cutlets are pounded to a quarter-inch, the distance from the oil to the geometric center is small enough that conducted heat reaches 165°F almost as soon as the crust finishes browning.',
    keywords: ['how long to fry chicken cutlets in skillet', 'pan fried breaded chicken time', 'skillet chicken milanese temperature', 'crispy chicken cutlets on stove', 'chicken cutlet internal temp'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to cook breaded chicken cutlets in a skillet: 5–7 min in 350°F shallow oil. Wire rack resting prevents soggy crusts.',
