      'The heavy lid must fit tightly enough to maintain gentle steam recirculation during stovetop simmering — any gap will cool the pot faster than the burner can recover, forcing you to raise heat and risk a hard boil that breaks apart the delicate thigh meat. Test the lid by tilting the pot; it should stay sealed under its own weight.',
      'Position the Dutch oven across two burners if your pot is 5+ quarts, or use the largest single burner on your stove. Set heat to the level that produces steady rolling bubbles under the lid (roughly 325°F liquid temperature), not a raging boil that lifts the lid or a bare simmer with thin steam.',
