        a: 'The skin is edible; it\'s flavorful collagen-rich tissue that has softened to a slippery, tender texture after the braise. Many cooks eat it directly or chop it and stir it back into the soup. If the skin tastes overly smoky or salty, discard it, but there\'s no food safety issue.',
