    technicalDeepDive: 'Three proteins share one endpoint only because their safe minimums overlap: 165°F satisfies the USDA reheating temperature for cooked duck confit, clears the whole-cut pork minimum, and clears the ground-sausage minimum too, so one target works for all three at once. The dry beans rely on sustained moist heat to soften the pectin binding their cell walls, a slower process than protein denaturation, which is why they get a head start with an overnight soak and parcook before the rest of the dish goes in. Baking uncovered at 300°F exposes the surface to dry convective heat instead of trapping steam under a lid, letting a browned crust form across the top.',
