      'Watch for small white beads forming on the flesh surface as it nears done — that\'s rendered intramuscular fat pushing up through the muscle segments, and a light scattering of it is expected, but a heavy, continuous weep across the whole surface means it\'s already past medium.',
      'Listen for the sizzle to shift from a wetter hiss to a drier, slightly crackling sound partway through the skin-down stage — that\'s the fat layer under the skin finishing its render, and it tends to arrive a little before the skin physically releases from the grate.',
