    proTip: 'Orient the steak on the grate with the tenderloin lobe facing the cooler zone — the filet side sits inside a smaller cross-section and cooks 8–10°F ahead of the strip side, so treating both sides as one steak leaves the tenderloin overcooked by the time the strip is medium-rare. Probing next to the bone gives a false low reading because the bone insulates; probe the geometric centre of the strip lobe instead.',
