    verificationBasis: 'USDA FSIS 165°F poultry safe minimum; Crock-Pot 6-Qt "Set & Forget" cooking chart (bone-in chicken thighs 5–6 hrs LOW); the 175°F shred pull-target for dark meat is standard across ATK "Slow Cooker Revolution" and Serious Eats braised-thigh references; jarred salsa verde acidity (tomatillo-based, pH ~3.8) is documented on Herdez and Frontera nutrition panels.',
    technicalDeepDive: 'Thigh meat carries noticeably more intramuscular fat and connective tissue than breast, both of which render and hydrolyze over the LOW cycle to baste the fibers from the inside, which is what lets this cut safely climb well past the poultry minimum without drying out. Leaving the bone in slows heat penetration right at the joint, so the thickest, densest part of the thigh spends more time in the temperature band where collagen breaks down rather than racing ahead of the surrounding meat. The tomatillo salsa\'s acidity works on that surface layer throughout, gradually loosening the muscle nearest the sauce.',
    keywords: ['how long to slow cook salsa verde chicken', 'chicken verde slow cooker time', 'crockpot salsa verde chicken thighs', 'slow cooker green chile chicken', 'salsa verde chicken internal temp'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to cook salsa verde chicken in the slow cooker: 5–6 hours on LOW to a 175°F thigh. Why stirring mid-cook wrecks the shred.',
