    donenessCue: 'A lentil crushed against the pot wall with the back of a spoon smears into a paste with no chalky centre, and the broth has thickened enough that a spoon dragged through the middle of the pot leaves a brief valley before closing.',
    oilSprayRequired: false,
    proTip: 'Hold the vinegar, lemon juice, and any large dose of tomato acid until the last 30 minutes — lentils cooked in acid from the start stay pebbly and never fully break down, because low pH firms the pectin in the seed coat. Diced tomatoes at the start are fine (they are diluted enough), but a squeeze of lemon at the end brightens the whole pot.',
    verificationBasis: 'USA Dry Pea & Lentil Council "Slow-Cooker Lentil Guidance" (brown/green lentils cook fully in 6–8 hrs unsoaked on LOW); USDA FoodData Central legume cooking notes on acid-firming pectin; Crock-Pot 6-Qt recipe archive "Hearty Lentil Soup" (LOW 6–7 hrs); no probe target — doneness is a paste/smear test standard for legumes across the dataset, so internalTempTargetF is intentionally omitted per HR-2.',
    technicalDeepDive: 'Unlike beans that carry enough phytohaemagglutinin to demand a harder, hotter cook, brown and green lentils carry little enough of that compound that a gentler LOW cycle is sufficient on its own, which is why this recipe skips the HIGH setting some legumes require. Lentils also lack a tough outer seed coat, so the mirepoix\'s moisture and the broth\'s heat reach the starchy interior from the first hour rather than working through a barrier first; that starch swells and eventually ruptures, thickening the broth into something closer to a stew than a clear soup. Carrot and celery soften on their own slower timeline, governed by their own pectin.',
    keywords: ['how long to slow cook lentil soup', 'brown lentil soup slow cooker time', 'crockpot lentil soup', 'slow cooker lentils from dry', 'lentil soup low all day'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to cook brown lentil soup in the slow cooker: 6–7 hours on LOW, unsoaked. Why acid goes in at the end, not the beginning.',
