    technicalDeepDive: 'Chuck comes from the shoulder clod, one of the most exercised and collagen-dense areas on the animal, and only a sustained eight-to-nine-hour hold gives that tissue enough time to fully break down into gelatin; pulled early, the same fibers that shred cleanly at hour eight would instead resist the fork. The stick of butter melts down through the roast by gravity long before the meat itself is tender, so by the time the chuck is ready its fibers have already been sitting in rendered fat for most of the cook. The salt in the ranch and au jus packets meanwhile diffuses slowly inward through the meat over those same hours, working like a slow-motion wet brine.',
    keywords: ['how long to slow cook mississippi pot roast', 'mississippi roast crockpot time', 'slow cooker mississippi pot roast', 'pepperoncini pot roast slow cooker', 'mississippi roast internal temp'],
