      'The sizzle is an audio cue for pan temperature—it should be constant and loud while the medallion cooks. If the sizzle drops to a faint hiss mid-cook, the pan temperature dropped and the second side won\'t brown evenly. Cover with a lid for 30 seconds to recover heat if this happens.',
      'Don\'t rely on surface colour alone for doneness. The internal pink band is the actual signal: cut a test medallion at the 5-minute mark and look for a thin translucent blush in the very centre. If it\'s still white and opaque throughout, cook another 30–60 seconds per side.',
