      'Within 10-15 seconds of hitting room air, the edges will visibly collapse inward as steam cools and the structure loses buoyancy. This collapse is not failure but the normal physics of cooling. If the interior was actually at 200-205°F, the center will remain relatively high even after this edge collapse.',
