    verificationBasis: 'Instant Brands Official Cooking Time Chart (Fruit → Applesauce entry: 5 min HP for cut apples, published in the Duo/Duo Plus/Pro user manuals and on instantpot.com); USDA FoodData Central apple composition data (pectin softens above 183°F, well within HP chamber conditions); no internal-temp target — HR-2 permits omitting internalTempTargetF for fruit where doneness is a texture cue.',
    technicalDeepDive: 'Apple flesh is mostly water held together by pectin in the walls between cells; heat doesn\'t really cook the fruit so much as dissolve that pectin, letting cells slip apart from one another. Because the chunks are small and already saturated with moisture, steam near 239°F conducts through them in minutes and pushes the pectin past its softening point, with no dense muscle fiber or starch granule slowing that diffusion the way there is in a roast or a dry bean. Five minutes collapses the outer layer of each chunk into pulp while a firmer core survives, giving pressure-cooked applesauce its rustic texture instead of a uniform puree.',
    keywords: ['how long to cook applesauce in instant pot', 'instant pot applesauce time', 'pressure cooker applesauce', 'instant pot chunky applesauce', 'homemade applesauce instant pot'],
    metaDescription: 'How long to cook applesauce in the Instant Pot from raw apples: 5 mins High Pressure + quick release. Why blending 2 varieties beats using one.',
