        prevention: 'The thermometer confirms food safety (160°F kills pathogenic bacteria in ground beef), but doneness is determined by the sauce\'s texture and clinginess, not the temperature. Keep the simmer going until the glaze is visibly thickened and clinging to each crumble, even if that takes an extra minute past the time window.',
