        prevention: 'Cast iron\'s thermal mass keeps the surface temperature stable even after the cold fillet lands on it, ensuring even browning across the entire skin. If cast iron is unavailable, use the heaviest stainless steel pan you have, preheat it 1–2 minutes longer than you would cast iron, and increase the heat setting slightly.',
