    technicalDeepDive: 'Pounding the breast to a quarter inch shortens the conduction path to the center, so myosin and actin finish denaturing to a safe internal temperature in roughly the same window the crust needs to lock, instead of leaving undercooked meat beneath a finished crust. The egg wash\'s proteins coagulate almost immediately in the hot oil, cementing the breadcrumb matrix to the meat surface before it can slip loose during frying. Dry heat conduction through the oil also drives off surface moisture fast enough that the crumb dehydrates and browns via Maillard reactions rather than steaming under its own trapped moisture.',
