      'Keep thighs skin-side up for the entire cook rather than flipping partway through as you might with a steak or rack of ribs; chicken skin needs uninterrupted exposure to chamber convection to render and crisp, and time spent skin-down against the grate just steams it instead.',
      'Leave at least an inch of open grate between thighs. Skin-on poultry sheds a surprising volume of fat as it renders, and thighs set too close let that fat pool between them, holding the touching edges of skin in a wet, rubbery state instead of letting it drain and crisp.',
