      'Insert the probe horizontally into the thickest lobe of meat from the side rather than pushing it straight down through the skin. A straight-down puncture opens a channel through the exact layer that\'s supposed to seal fat in and crisp, letting both fat and juice escape through the hole.',
      'Because these thighs spend a comparatively short 75 to 90 minutes in the chamber rather than many hours, a milder fruitwood like apple or cherry suits them better than a heavier wood such as hickory or mesquite — there isn\'t enough time in this shorter cook for a stronger wood\'s sharper compounds to mellow out.',
