        q: 'A bratwurst split slightly during cooking but didn\'t fully rupture. Are they still safe and how does this affect texture?',
        a: 'Yes, completely safe if the internal temperature reached 160°F. A small tear means some liquid escaped, so that section will be slightly drier than a perfectly intact sausage, but the difference is usually minor if caught quickly.',
