      'Using an independent oven thermometer (even if your oven has a built-in dial) is worthwhile for pot roasting; the braise is extremely sensitive to 10-15°F swings, and ovens often run 15-25°F hotter or cooler than their dial suggests. At 315°F, the braise stretches past 240 minutes; at 335°F, you risk over-tenderizing the collagen.',
