        q: 'Should I sear the roast on all sides or just the top before braising?',
        a: 'Sear all six sides (top, bottom, and four long edges) to build fond on all the surfaces that will touch the pot and to develop a complete caramelized crust that contributes depth to the jus; if you sear only the top and bottom, the long edges will have a steamed appearance and contribute less flavor to the braising liquid.',
