        consequence: 'Each lid-lift drops the internal pot temperature by 20–30°F and releases the low-pressure steam environment that accelerates protein breakdown. The braising liquid evaporates faster, and cook time extends by 5–8 minutes per interruption—you end up basting constantly and still waiting for doneness.',
        prevention: 'Commit to the timer. Check doneness only once at the 40-minute mark using an instant-read probe inserted at the thickest link\'s center, and accept whatever temperature you find. If below 155°F, recover with a re-covered braise for another 5–8 minutes and re-check. Resist the urge to verify plumpness or juice clarity visually.',
