      'Shape the patties slightly thinner in the center than at the edges (about 1/4-inch at the thinnest point, 3/8-inch at the rim), so the edges firm first—this lets you flip or check the bottom without the center pressing out and breaking the patty. Uniform thickness means the center is still fragile when the edges are set.',
