      'The patty\'s exterior should transition from tan to a light golden-brown; at 165°F (the safe endpoint), the outside color typically looks like a well-toasted bread crust, not like a medium-rare beef burger. Ground turkey won\'t develop the caramel-brown that a ribeye does because it lacks the Maillard-conducive fats.',
      'Press the center of a patty with tongs or a spatula—a fully cooked turkey burger at 165°F should give slightly under pressure but spring back, and should feel noticeably firmer than when you first placed it in the fryer. If it\'s still squishy like a raw burger, it\'s not done.',
