      'The transition from stovetop to oven is significant: medium-low stovetop heat sits around 300°F, but the 400°F oven is a 100-degree jump that will aggressively brown skin already started on the stovetop. Place the pan on the middle oven rack, not the top, so the skin experiences more indirect radiant heat and less direct top-flame intensity that risks blackening.',
