        a: 'Tenderloins smaller than 1 lb are too thin to form a proper Maillard crust in the 6-minute sear without over-cooking the interior. Tenderloins larger than 1.5 lb are awkwardly thick in the center and would require a much longer oven time (20–25 minutes), risking an over-browned exterior. The 1–1.25 lb range is the sweet spot for even cooking with good browning in the given time.',
