        q: 'Do I need to soak brown lentils overnight like I do with dried beans?',
        a: 'No. Brown lentils have thin seed coats compared to other legumes, and their starch granules absorb water readily during cooking without a pre-soak. Soaking actually wastes time and offers no texture benefit—you will get the same creamy result in 40–45 minutes unsoaked as you would in 30 minutes with a 12-hour soak.',
