        q: 'What is the difference between creamy throughout and blowouts when I look at the lentils?',
        a: 'Creamy throughout means when you break a lentil open, the interior is uniformly soft and pale (from gelatinized starch), and the hull stays intact and flakes off cleanly. Blowouts are lentils where the hull has cracked and split apart, with starch leaking into the broth—the lentil fragments float separately and the broth turns starchy and thick. You want zero or maybe one blowout per pot.',
