      'If a half is large enough that its cut face also touches the sloped side wall of the insert and not just the water pool at the bottom, angle it so most of the cut surface sits over the water rather than wedged against the ceramic wall — direct wall contact conducts heat faster than the steam above the water does, and can turn that edge mushy before the center of the same half finishes.',
