      'The rub here is pure cracked pepper and coriander with no added salt, since the meat is already cured; press it on by hand into the still-damp desalted surface rather than using a mustard or oil binder, which the naturally tacky surface doesn\'t need and which can dull the peppery color of the finished bark.',
      'A brisket flat carries only a thin fat cap compared to a full packer, so if any cap remains, orient it toward the main heat source (the firebox side on an offset, or simply up in a vertical or pellet unit) so what little fat is present renders down through the leaner muscle instead of dripping away unused.',
