        q: 'Can you boil gnocchi from frozen without thawing them first?',
        a: 'Yes, frozen gnocchi cook through with an extra 30 to 45 seconds, but the floating signal becomes less reliable because ice crystal structure alters how steam builds inside the dough. Thaw them in the refrigerator for 2 to 3 hours before cooking if you want the standard 2-to-3-minute window and the reliable float test.',
