      'Position the pot lid so it sits directly on the rim rather than tilted or partially ajar; condensation running down the lid\'s underside and dripping back into the stew can cool the broth if the seal is loose, and uneven steam distribution underneath means some dumplings puff while others stay dense.',
      'If your stew has a thick fat layer on top (from chicken thighs or dark meat), skim most of it before dropping dumplings; while fat enriches flavor, an inch of it acts as an insulator that slows steam circulation and can result in dumplings that look puffed on top but remain doughy in the middle.',
