      'Dumplings that did not rise to full size often stayed sunken in the broth; if you see a partial dumpling still halfway submerged after 15 minutes, it means it was underblended batter (too wet and heavy) rather than undercooked, and opening the lid now will collapse the risen ones without saving the failed one.',
      'The bottom edge of the pot where broth meets the side will show a faint ring of tiny bubbles rising slowly if temperature is holding steady at 195°F; if those bubbles stop and the broth surface goes flat-calm, heat has dropped and dumplings have likely stalled partway through their rise.',
