    technicalDeepDive: 'Ground turkey exposes far more surface area than a whole cut, since grinding ruptures muscle fibers and spreads myoglobin throughout rather than confining it to a solid mass, so heat conducts through fast and coagulates protein quickly at 195°F. Because the meat is lean, the target stops right at the USDA 165°F minimum rather than climbing further, since extra minutes past that point would drive out moisture the low fat content cannot replace. The cannellini beans run on a separate clock: their starch granules need the same 35 to 40 minutes of contact with hot liquid to absorb water and gelatinize, which is what thickens the broth.',
